    "formal_inputs": "Nodes categorized formal_input are nonexecuting, synthetic interface values with initial definitions; they have no CFG vertices. Each has source-order position and retained parameter kind.",
    "definition_tuple": ["definition ID", "symbol alias", "defining node alias"],
    "symbol_tuple": ["symbol alias", "declared source name", "resolved type", "role", "declaring identifier selector"],
    "cfg_edge_tuple": ["source alias", "target alias", "CFG kind"],
    "reaching_definition_edge_tuple": ["defining node", "read node", "definition ID"],
    "reaching_definition_attributes": "kind=data, subkind=reaching_definition, operand_position=0, symbol_id from definition, loop_carried=false",
    "value_edge_tuple": ["producer", "consumer", "operand position"],
    "value_attributes": "kind=data, subkind=value_operand; no definition_id; omit every unit-typed transferred value even when explicitly produced. Retain unit binding reaching_definition edges and source operations; no unit merges or unit value_alternative edges.",
    "alternative_edge_tuple": ["producer", "merge", "alternative position", "outcome", "controller"],
    "alternative_attributes": "kind=data, subkind=value_alternative; positions true=0/false=1; annotations[compat.rust.hir-r0:guards] mirrors the alternative in value_sites. One edge per semantic producer/merge/position/outcome, never one per completion frontier member or guard term.",
        "guards": "compat.rust.hir-r0:guards is a DNF array of conjunction arrays of atoms {controller_pdg_node_id,outcome}, with outcome true/false strings. [] is impossible; [[]] is unconditional. An atom requires its controller to have executed and selected that outcome. Value-site annotations mirror merge-node annotations; alternative annotations mirror value_alternative edge annotations.",
    "execution_edge_tuple": ["prerequisite", "target"],
    "execution_attributes": "kind=execution, subkind=nearest_dominating_operation",
    "control_edge_tuple": ["controller", "controlled operation", "outcome"],
    "control_attributes": "kind=control, subkind=postdominance",
    "local_definition_sets": "Exact per-symbol IN sets at the listed CFG operations, and exact generated OUT sets after each listed write. read_definitions lists the entire IN set for that read. No hidden phi/definition is permitted.",
    "exactness": "For every case with exact_graph=true, node inventory, reachable CFG transfers, all three reachable PDG edge families and definitions are exact multisets, not subsets. No unspecified exec/control/data edges are allowed. Derive required source spans, original kinds, operator/literal/write attributes, policy and provenance from the normative profile; aliases are not semantic labels. Unreachable diagnostic operand edges are specified separately if retained.",
